// The negative space of the mangled-name lookup bypass. Skipping the namespace
// filter is only sound because a mangled name spells its whole path, so two
// same-named module types in different namespaces mangle differently
// (fc__alpha__cfg__rec vs fc__beta__cfg__rec) and cannot merge. Both shapes
// below are named `cfg.rec` and differ in layout, so a mix-up is a wrong answer
// rather than a silent tie. (a_alpha.fc sorts first, so alpha's `rec` registers
// first; the consumer's second field targets beta's.)
namespace alpha::

module cfg =
    struct rec =
        v: i32
